 "q-341576/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "488bc865-d437-563b-95d6-2139e3e2a8b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341576/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0c78726-f95b-5d89-8616-a46065fdb064" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341576/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-341576/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-341576/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341576" :question/id #uuid "2e581ab1-1c0e-5e8a-a3db-36c8d21f3746" :question/math-academy-id "q-341576" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/ef59e4b5c39770c5bcade3475a23d2631d2db10fea4fd7c925be092bbf819e61.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is not continuous but is right-continuous at\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=c,$ we need to check whether the right-sided limit is equal to the function value.\n\nThe function has three discontinuities: $x=-1$ and $x=3.$\n\n- At $x=-1$ the function is right-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}f(x)=1=f(-1).\\,✓\n$$\n\n- At $x=3$ the function is not right-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{3}^{+}}f(x)=-1\\ne 1=f(3).\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is not continuous but is right-continuous at $x=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341576/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff9486fe-3ee1-5917-88de-97251c889552"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341576"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341375/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "ea9ad21e-441b-55ea-8219-051fd4298f44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341375/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "30f95881-1911-5674-bb10-e4c875e39d4d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341375/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-341375/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341375/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "b8960d1d-052a-50ff-88f3-364a4c6c5c23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341375/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "13031d09-e88f-5c61-bf6d-c5d64d7aedcb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341375/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-341375/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341375" :question/id #uuid "d7444952-e689-5026-9ea6-0702c532dc85" :question/math-academy-id "q-341375" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/f223c6b96b4ce7e522d1529145ae90d7d68927e3234aa891a7be30a345355a9e.png)\n\nFrom **left to right**, the function $y=f(x)$ above is left-continuous but is not continuous at\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}} $\\,$ and  \n$\\,x=$\n {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=c,$ we need to check whether the left-sided limit is equal to the function value.\n\nThe function has three discontinuities: $x=-2,$ $x=1,$ and $x=3.$\n\n- At $x=-2$ the function is not left-continuous because it's undefined at this point. $\\,\\times $\n\n- At $x=1$ the function is left-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x)=2=f(1).\\,✓\n$$\n\n- At $x=3$ the function is left-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{3}^{-}}f(x)=0=f(3).\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, from **left to right**, the function $f(x)$ is not continuous but is right-continuous at $x=1$ and $x=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341375/field-1" "q-341375/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff9486fe-3ee1-5917-88de-97251c889552"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341375"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73054/selection/8dd0139fe2bdff82a7de02af21e81b3fb0031e695d60709e4cec3b9cfa395bee" :answer/id #uuid "d533677d-2133-54c8-b120-817beeccc476" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-1$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73054/selection/be41bc64385bf521340524b4e278e6df8cc0ad1e10dce19632624b00d7fa202b" :answer/id #uuid "2f897499-a605-584e-8b8b-0ed17601335c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-1$ and $x=1$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73054/selection/565f087efc172cc689d6ac7a38ae1818e245a6f8995ecba68bcdf0ac5950b2ea" :answer/id #uuid "86f28d33-c9f1-586f-bb7e-be126639db77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=1$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73054/selection/82d8beec48d8e7000728fc93bb99e8896041037eb2d23f8dc73b025ed9a4e82c" :answer/id #uuid "990b81df-e422-5c50-94fa-05c0ae079607" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=1$ and $x=3$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73054/selection/54ac610d4774fee0ede6478b691a6eacc7c927529e978f51a18e757cb18525eb" :answer/id #uuid "f72829e6-9b0c-5ffb-af82-22f6fe043c9b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=3$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73054/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "99efa492-d17b-5f74-8def-5881e270cf91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73054/selection/54ac610d4774fee0ede6478b691a6eacc7c927529e978f51a18e757cb18525eb" :answer-field/choices ["q-73054/selection/8dd0139fe2bdff82a7de02af21e81b3fb0031e695d60709e4cec3b9cfa395bee" "q-73054/selection/be41bc64385bf521340524b4e278e6df8cc0ad1e10dce19632624b00d7fa202b" "q-73054/selection/565f087efc172cc689d6ac7a38ae1818e245a6f8995ecba68bcdf0ac5950b2ea" "q-73054/selection/82d8beec48d8e7000728fc93bb99e8896041037eb2d23f8dc73b025ed9a4e82c" "q-73054/selection/54ac610d4774fee0ede6478b691a6eacc7c927529e978f51a18e757cb18525eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73054" :question/id #uuid "23d077ae-b48b-5fdf-8116-b40f9d5a2533" :question/math-academy-id "q-73054" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/a025dc971bd0bb473e6b47f90b68ee8e8573a7acc8e5e879eab0173be1d41dcb.png)\n\nAt which points is the function $y=f(x)$ above left-continuous but is not continuous?" :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=c,$ we need to check whether the left-sided limit is equal to the function value.\n\nLet's check this for $x=-1$, at $x=1$ and at  $x=3.$\n\n- At $x=-1$ the function is not left-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}f(x)=1\\ne -1=f(-1).\n$$\n\n- At $x=1$ the function is not left-continuous because \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x)=-1\\ne 1=f(1).\n$$\n\n- At $x=3$ the function is left-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{3}^{-}}f(x)=1=f(3).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=3$ only." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73054/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff9486fe-3ee1-5917-88de-97251c889552"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73054"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341379/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "724420fc-6fa0-5034-b16a-c970cec521e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341379/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "36e772ba-52d9-52b3-a48e-7ddf83af5b76" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341379/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-341379/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341379/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "8c31086e-5f9d-542a-8ac5-193b4a7832dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341379/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "fed81b16-5ce8-5842-85b3-f808e335dd19" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341379/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-341379/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341379" :question/id #uuid "e3dbf1cc-f8fe-5c56-b884-f7d15af77f72" :question/math-academy-id "q-341379" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/f4f20d86a96988d657aeac166b6228cc938523e0ba6100908725aa83b6c88781.png)\n\nFrom **left to right**, the function $y=f(x)$ above is not continuous but is right-continuous at\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}} $\\,$ and  \n$\\,x=$\n {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=c,$ we need to check whether the right-sided limit is equal to the function value.\n\nThe function has three discontinuities: $x=-3$, $x=-1,$ and $x=1.$\n\n- At $x=-3$ the function is right-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{+}}f(x)=-2=f(-3).\\,✓\n$$\n\n- At $x=-1$ the function is not right-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}f(x)=0\\ne -2=f(-1).\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- At $x=1$ the function is right-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x)=0=f(1).\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, from **left to right**, the function $f(x)$ is not continuous but is right-continuous at\n$x=-3$ and $x=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341379/field-1" "q-341379/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff9486fe-3ee1-5917-88de-97251c889552"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341379"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104285/selection/ed46a7ab66f4e1f0492ab8ee0b3b7d22df7bff44011d5a9f713d6c9393035ddc" :answer/id #uuid "84ce691c-0b18-5fe2-b430-28c925561502" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "49" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104285/selection/ffd075d9f78bc91ad1230b13b8ccd1d00ef82102ef3fbce7f8814aaaa75a623d" :answer/id #uuid "8a7361fa-3bd2-5829-b0da-40975f839aed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "169" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104285/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "5bd419f7-d872-57d3-bfee-9f241feafe62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104285/selection/ea469f3e53b818ab5b703dc09f193c7093ac0666865c0a5b323c43d7b199b090" :answer/id #uuid "b972fc2f-51d3-5e72-bf75-32cd8beadf13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "144" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104285/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer/id #uuid "d3c3c0aa-0999-5613-bfcb-97e3ffc6d1c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104285/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c249743-73da-5b32-a686-f0c5727d5e79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104285/selection/ffd075d9f78bc91ad1230b13b8ccd1d00ef82102ef3fbce7f8814aaaa75a623d" :answer-field/choices ["q-104285/selection/ed46a7ab66f4e1f0492ab8ee0b3b7d22df7bff44011d5a9f713d6c9393035ddc" "q-104285/selection/ffd075d9f78bc91ad1230b13b8ccd1d00ef82102ef3fbce7f8814aaaa75a623d" "q-104285/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-104285/selection/ea469f3e53b818ab5b703dc09f193c7093ac0666865c0a5b323c43d7b199b090" "q-104285/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104285" :question/id #uuid "74f21211-cc3c-54cf-8784-8fd096842237" :question/math-academy-id "q-104285" :question/problem "If $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=-9$ and $f(-9)=4,$ then what is \n${lim}_{x\\to (-9)^{-}}(f(x)-x)^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=-9,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-9)^{-}}f(x)=f(-9)=4.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-9)^{-}}(f(x)-x)^{2}=(4-(-9))^{2}=169.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104285/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dc967c7-840e-5717-98f2-330fcf0fe12d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104285"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339592/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "bf7d4618-52eb-519a-b7d5-479a6da2c3a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339592/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6f982f4b-0a43-5957-a096-7ed259b0a574" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339592/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5c5832d-07e2-595d-afe1-ac6be838fa8e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339592/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-339592/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-339592/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339592" :question/id #uuid "6c3e571a-4724-5af9-bcc0-f9ca20412934" :question/math-academy-id "q-339592" :question/problem "If $g(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=5$ and $g(5)=5,$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}\\frac{g(x)-{x}^{2}}{4x}=$\n {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since $g(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=5,$ we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}g(x)=g(5)=5.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}\\frac{g(x)-{x}^{2}}{4x} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}g(x)-\\text{ }{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}{x}^{2}}{{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}4x} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-{5}^{2}}{4(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-25}{20} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339592/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dc967c7-840e-5717-98f2-330fcf0fe12d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339592"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339585/field-1/2ac375c4f78a87c501effe61daec77cdf9edaee2a52a73363e0d0a0e421862d4" :answer/id #uuid "0acdea37-b24e-5d1b-85c2-287592cf22dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339585/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "01aacdc2-7e87-599a-bde9-7f9c7ea4a42b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339585/field-1/2ac375c4f78a87c501effe61daec77cdf9edaee2a52a73363e0d0a0e421862d4" :answer-field/choices ["q-339585/field-1/2ac375c4f78a87c501effe61daec77cdf9edaee2a52a73363e0d0a0e421862d4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339585" :question/id #uuid "3ef9c30f-4a7e-5e86-9fd3-8b9955c73729" :question/math-academy-id "q-339585" :question/problem "If $g(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=10$ and $g(10)=5,$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {10}^{+}}\\frac{g(x)-\\operatorname{log}⁡x}{3g(10)}=$\n {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since $g(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=10,$ we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{+}}g(x)=g(10)=5.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{+}}\\frac{g(x)-\\operatorname{log}⁡x}{3g(10)} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{+}}g(x)-{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{+}}\\operatorname{log}⁡x}{3g(10)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-\\operatorname{log}⁡10}{3(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-1}{3(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339585/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dc967c7-840e-5717-98f2-330fcf0fe12d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339597/field-1/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" :answer/id #uuid "347740f4-fe94-500c-870d-738b6323e770" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339597/field-1/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c" :answer/id #uuid "19d48e51-e895-517b-9a09-d87b29aaba2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "150" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339597/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "23495c8d-030c-57a0-9a16-a93380bb783c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339597/field-1/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" :answer-field/choices ["q-339597/field-1/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" "q-339597/field-1/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339597" :question/id #uuid "224c62c3-d8c3-5a74-a48f-f28670c74d80" :question/math-academy-id "q-339597" :question/problem "If $h(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=10$ and $h(10)=15,$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}(xh(x)-5h(10))=$\n {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since $h(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=10,$ we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}h(x)=h(10)=15.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}(xh(x)-5h(10)) & ={lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}x\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}h(x)-5\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}h(10) \\\\  & =10\\cdot 15-5\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =150-75 \\\\  & =75.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339597/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dc967c7-840e-5717-98f2-330fcf0fe12d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339597"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38328"] :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=2,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)=f(2)=-1.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}(f(x)+f(2)) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)+f(2) \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-38546/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "3afb8365-ed02-5316-b45a-395ca92a0387" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38546/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "35e513e2-4478-554b-87f5-f313666b3fc3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38546/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "8b6329c6-37d6-5df0-bab7-63762383b3ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38546/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "ce6e9156-4ccf-53c2-bb5c-a1e91ccb29