 $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=3,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}f(x)=3\\ne 1=f(3)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=3,$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}f(x)=1=f(3)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=3,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not left-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73105/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73105"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104357/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "28a07236-8fc2-52a3-a627-eec7c5aa3925" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104357/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "6dba1311-cb9b-503f-b9cf-793ab31e4a87" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104357/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "5a67c79c-749c-5e54-ae82-c55a357465b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104357/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "9fd73b91-058d-52cc-8867-1a5761d5c95f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104357/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927